{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The method scales as O(d^3) in FLOP complexity and parameter count, surpassing the super‑exponential scaling of mHC‑lite and KromHC’s component factors.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000024"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "O(d^3)",
        "mHC-lite",
        "KromHC"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": null,
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000024"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The method requires no custom CUDA kernels, relying only on batched linear solves and tensor contractions.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000025"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "CUDA kernels",
        "batched linear solves",
        "tensor contractions"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The method achieves exact double stochasticity by construction, with no iterations and no approximation gap.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000026"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "double stochasticity"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The method includes a hyperparameter s that interpolates between the orthostochastic boundary (s=1) and the dense interior of the Birkhoff polytope (s→∞).",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000027"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "hyperparameter s",
        "orthostochastic boundary",
        "Birkhoff polytope"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The method provides a potential avenue for scaling Hyper‑Connections with tractable complexity while maintaining significant expressivity.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000028"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Hyper‑Connections",
        "expressivity"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The method can be used simultaneously with KromHC to allow for larger Kronecker factors by mitigating the super‑exponential scaling introduced in mHC‑lite.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000028"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "KromHC",
        "Kronecker factors",
        "mHC‑lite"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "2 Related Work",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000029"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Residual connections and their generalizations.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000030"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "He et al. introduced skip connections that enable gradient flow via identity shortcuts in ResNets.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000031"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "He et al.",
        "skip connections",
        "ResNets"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Skip connections are a key component in the design of large language models (LLMs) owing to their stability and scalability.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000031"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "large language models",
        "LLMs"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "DenseNet, FractalNet, and subsequent works explored richer connectivity patterns passing intermediate features across networks.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000031"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "DenseNet",
        "FractalNet"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Various works have explored novel ways of increasing the effective size of the residual stream, such as ResiDual and AltUp.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000031"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "ResiDual",
        "AltUp"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Hyper‑Connections (HC) introduced the first learnable, multi‑stream generalization of residual streams allowing for dynamic mixing matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000032"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "Hyper‑Connections"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "dynamic mixing matrices"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "HC can theoretically enable models to learn depth and width connections, dynamically rearrange layer connectivity and potentially adds a new avenue for scaling.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000032"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "depth connections",
        "width connections",
        "scaling"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Later works have expanded on HC by splitting the feature dimension into independent sub‑streams and applying HC to vision and graph neural networks.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000032"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "vision",
        "graph neural networks"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The unconstrained dynamic connectivity of residual blocks in HC removes the explicit guarantee of the identity property, introducing the risk of gradient instability after repeated applications of the mixing terms.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000033"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "gradient instability",
        "mixing terms"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "This instability impacts deep networks and restricts scalability due to vanishing and exploding gradients.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000033"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "vanishing gradients",
        "exploding gradients"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Subsequent works investigate constraining this connectivity to a manifold that bounds gradient updates through the spectral norm in order to address this instability.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000033"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "manifold",
        "spectral norm"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Manifold‑Constrained Hyper‑Connections.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000034"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Manifold‑Constrained Hyper‑Connections (mHC) constrain the dynamic residual matrices to a manifold to improve training stability while still allowing for dynamic connections.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000035"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "Manifold‑Constrained Hyper‑Connections",
        "mHC"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "training stability",
        "dynamic connections"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "mHC primarily changes the definition of ℋ_l^res such that it converges to the Birkhoff polytope B_d, the closed set of doubly stochastic matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000035"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "ℋ_l^res",
        "Birkhoff polytope",
        "B_d"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "B_d denotes the closed set of doubly stochastic matrices, defined as positive matrices with the property M^T J_d = M J_d = J_d.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000036"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "B_d"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "doubly stochastic matrices",
        "M",
        "J_d"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": null,
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000036"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "J_d denotes the d×d ones matrix.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000037"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "J_d"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "ones matrix"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "mHC attempts to enforce the doubly stochastic constraint after weight updates using the Sinkhorn‑Knopp (SK) algorithm.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000038"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Sinkhorn‑Knopp",
        "SK algorithm"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Implementing the SK kernel requires careful kernel‑level optimization for efficiency.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000038"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "kernel‑level optimization"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Finite SK iterations introduce an approximation gap that accumulates with network depth.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000038"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "approximation gap",
        "network depth"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "mHC‑lite attempts to circumvent the approximation gap and customized kernel by making use of the Birkhoff–von Neumann theorem to define the learned connections as a convex combination of d! permutation matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000039"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "mHC‑lite"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Birkhoff–von Neumann theorem",
        "permutation matrices"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "mHC‑lite has a computational cost of O(d C · d!).",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000039"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "computational cost",
        "O(d C · d!)"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": null,
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000039"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "mHC‑lite works well for small d, however, it is not tenable in the limit of scaling d > 8.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000039"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "small d",
        "d > 8"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "KromHC sacrifices expressivity and complete coverage of B_d by using tensor products to train residual connections on a much smaller set of exactly double‑stochastic matrices, with a cost of O(d² C).",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000039"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "KromHC"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "tensor products",
        "double‑stochastic matrices",
        "O(d² C)"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": null,
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000039"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Cayley transforms in neural networks.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000040"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "The Cayley transform has been used to parameterize orthogonal matrices in recurrent networks.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000041"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Cayley transform",
        "orthogonal matrices",
        "recurrent networks"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Comparisons with the matrix exponential show similar quality and better stability at lower FLOP cost.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000041"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "matrix exponential",
        "FLOP cost"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Iterative Cayley‑based optimization outperforms matrix exponential approaches for Stiefel manifold problems.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000041"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "Stiefel manifold"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Doubly Stochastic & Orthostochastic matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000042"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Multiple works have investigated the use of doubly stochastic matrices in neural network parameterization.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000043"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "doubly stochastic matrices",
        "neural network parameterization"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Gutkin introduced generalized orthostochastic matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000043"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "generalized orthostochastic matrices"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Nechita et al. proved that the set of generalized s‑orthostochastic matrices is contained in B_d and spans all of B_d as s → ∞.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000043"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "s‑orthostochastic matrices",
        "B_d",
        "s → ∞"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "Other works have investigated further properties of the spectral span of the Birkhoff polytope and the geometry of s‑orthostochastic matrices in the quantum setting.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000043"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "spectral span",
        "Birkhoff polytope",
        "quantum setting"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "These theoretical foundations underlie our choice of parameterization.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000043"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "theoretical foundations",
        "parameterization"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "text": "To our knowledge, we are the first to apply this construction in a machine learning setting and, more specifically, to learned residual stream routing in deep networks.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000043"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [
        "residual stream routing",
        "deep networks"
      ],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "go‑mhC: Generalized Orthostochastic Manifold‑Constrained Hyper‑Connections",
